        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12480543/comment/12934464",
          "id": "12934464",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Hi Drew,\n\nI tried running {{ant generate-maven-artifacts}} without your patch, and I see the same failure as you do.\n\n(Actually, when I first tried, with Ant 1.8.1, it wasn't able to find the maven ant tasks jar (the most recent) that I had placed in {{$ANT_HOME/lib/}} - I downgraded to Ant 1.7.0 and everything went fine.  Apparently Ant 1.8.X no longer pays attention to jars in {{$ANT_HOME/lib/}}?)\n\nHowever, after applying your patch, the build still fails on trunk (haven't tried branch_3x yet), though not with the same failure.\n\n(Ant 1.7.0, Sun JDK 1.6.0_13 on Cygwin/WinVista):\n\n{noformat}\nBUILD FAILED\nC:\\cygwin\\home\\us\\svn\\lucene\\dev\\trunk\\lucene\\build.xml:396: The following error occurred while executing this line:\nC:\\cygwin\\home\\us\\svn\\lucene\\dev\\trunk\\lucene\\common-build.xml:324: Error deploying artifact 'org.apache.lucene:lucene-core:jar': Error deploying artifact: \nFile C:\\cygwin\\home\\us\\svn\\lucene\\dev\\trunk\\lucene\\build\\${project.artifactId}-${project.version}.jar does not exist\n{noformat}\n\nLooks like some kind of failed interpolation maybe?\n\nI'm going to try under Linux later today.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
