          "body": "Hudson nightly builds are failing when executing {{ant generate-maven-artifacts}}, with the same error as Drew reported.\n\nWhen I use {{maven-ant-tasks-2.0.9.jar}} with Ant 1.7.1 locally, and the equivalent of Drew's patches (since the POM parents have changed), I see the same errors, but the build doesn't fail.\n\nI just re-ran {{ant clean generate-maven-artifacts}} on trunk with an empty {{~/.m2/}} directory, Ant 1.7.1 and {{maven-ant-tasks-2.1.1.jar}} -- no errors were printed, and the build succeeded.\n\nI think instead of adding stuff to the *build.xml files, we should require {{maven-ant-tasks-2.1.1.jar}} for execution of {{ant generate-maven-artifacts}}.\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2011-01-21T17:39:05.286+0000",
          "updated": "2011-01-21T17:41:11.916+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12480543/comment/12984966",
          "id": "12984966",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "It appears that there were two problems blocking the Hudson build scripts from succeeding:\n\n# Maven Ant Tasks seems to dislike mixed artifact versions cached in the local maven repository ({{~/.m2/repository/}}) - this leads to errors that look like the one Drew originally reported on this issue, regardless of the version of Maven Ant Tasks that is used.\n# {{maven-ant-tasks-2.0.9.jar}} does not work with the new full POMs introduced by LUCENE-2657 - errors that look like Drew's are printed and the build fails.\n\nHowever, purging the local maven repository ({{~/.m2/repository/}}) and upgrading to {{maven-ant-tasks-2.1.1.jar}} allows {{ant generate-maven-artifacts}} to consistently succeed.\n\nUwe has changed the Hudson build setup to {{rm -rf $HOME/.m2/repository}} and has upgraded the Maven Ant Tasks jar to v2.1.1.  Since these changes, the only full build that has completed is the Lucene-3.x build, and it was a success.\n\nI'll leave this issue open until all of the nightly Hudson builds have succeeded (hopefully that will happen tonight).",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
